 "intro": [
  "Where the dead walk, the ground rots, and the rot is creeping north toward what is left of the Elderwold. The Thornwood Covenant has answered the only way it knows: Grovewarden Cerrid Ashbark is burning the edge of the fen, and the court's new graves with it.",
  "Tier 4 is open: wailing shades, which fly over the briars. While the Covenant holds all three of its camps, its burning bands come out of the trees again and again.",
  "Take Briarwatch and Elderfall, then drive Cerrid back from Ashbark Camp."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "saw_carvings"
   },
   "text": [
    "Cerrid escapes into the trees with half his warband. Among the ashes of a druid camp Corvin finds old carvings of a great stone held in a net of roots, the same as the stone in the clearing.",
    "\"They knew,\" he says. \"The roots held something shut, and the Concord cut them down.\""
   ]
  },
